    "bubble_choice_description": "Explore the Disney characters database API and create your own custom dashboard.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/0283296f6a7f6700f0a7056a714fe895-Screenshot 2026-01-28 at 1.08.22 PM.png",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore The Disney Characters Database\r\n\r\nSkim the official Disney Characters documentation in `documentation.md`. Then look at the JSON response for a single character in `disney.json` to figure out how the data is structured. \r\n\r\nUse AI Tutor to help you modify your code to display different information (like \"allies\" or \"TV shows\").\r\n\r\n_Hint: You can upload files like `disney.json` to use when prompting AI Tutor._\r\n\r\n:::details [Not sure how to modify the code?]\r\n\r\nTry one of the following prompts:\r\n\r\n- In the file `disney.json`, how do I access the \"vote\\_average\" to show the rating?\r\n- How do I change the code to display the \"release\\_date\" in a more readable format?\r\n- What is the difference between \"popularity\" and \"vote\\_count\"? \r\n:::",
